<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the top 10 movies at the box office for the Friday to Sunday period, according to studio estimates collected by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final data is due Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (1) 101 Dalmatians .............. $13.5 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Daylight .................... $10.2 million</p>
<p>    3 (2) Star Trek: First Contact ....  $6.7 million</p>
<p>    4=(4) Jingle All the Way ..........  $5.4 million</p>
<p>    4=(5) Ransom ......................  $5.4 million</p>
<p>    6 (3) Space Jam ...................  $4.4 million</p>
<p>    7 (7) The English Patient .........  $2.8 million</p>
<p>    8 (6) The Mirror Has Two Faces ....  $2.5 million</p>
<p>    9 (9) Romeo &amp; Juliet ..............  $1.2 million</p>
<p>   10(10) Set It Off ..................  $1.1 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Rank last week in parentheses.</p>
<p>&quot;101&quot; Dalmatians&quot; and &quot;Ransom&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co., &quot;Daylight&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd., &quot;Star Trek: First Contact&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc., &quot;Jingle All The Way&quot; and &quot;William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet&quot; are released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox. &quot;Space Jam&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc., &quot;The English Patient&quot; by Disney's Miramax Films. &quot;The Mirror Has Two Faces&quot; is released Sony Corp. and &quot;Set It Off&quot; is released by New Line Cinema, a unit of Time Warner.</p>
